-- title:
--   Special-fibre points of dimension ≤ 1 are generic
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and a package $\mathfrak{X}$ of Deligne–Rapoport model data for $X_0(p)$ over $\mathbb{Z}$ (a scheme `DRModel p` with its proper, flat, integral structure morphism to $\operatorname{Spec}\mathbb{Z}$, normality on affine opens, rational and geometric curve models with their compatibilities, the two cusp sections, the smooth locus, and the remaining fields of [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackage`](def/ModularCurve_DRModelPackage.html#L43)). Let $O$ be a discrete valuation domain whose maximal ideal is generated by the image of $p$, let $\kappa$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$, and let $\mathrm{to}\kappa : O \to \kappa$ be a ring homomorphism. Assume $H$, the hypotheses [`V3Asm.SiteHyps`](def/ModularCurve_ResolvedModelSite.html#L267): the node set of the fibre is finite, oriented crossing charts exist over the base change `bc`, the étale-neighbourhood data `EtNbhd` is given, the assignment of a node to its point of `XO` is injective with closed image points, and the model hypotheses `ModelHyps` hold. Assume moreover that each of the two distinguished points $\xi_j$ lies in the open `X0` of the chart input [`V3Asm.C`](def/ModularCurve_ResolvedModelSite.html#L280), the complement of the finitely many node points. Then for every point $y$ of the glued scheme $Y$ (the colimit of the glue diagram) which does not lie in the preimage under the structure morphism [`V3Asm.toBase`](def/ModularCurve_ResolvedModelSite.html#L287) to $\operatorname{Spec} O$ of the basic open $D(p)$ — that is, $y$ lies in the special fibre — and whose local ring has Krull dimension at most $1$, there is an index $v$ with $y = \eta(v)$, where $\eta$ is the family [`V3Asm.η`](def/ModularCurve_ResolvedModelSite.html#L407) of distinguished points of $Y$ attached to the strict and exceptional components.
--
--   This is the statement that the points of dimension at most one in the special fibre of the glued resolution are exactly among the prescribed generic points of its components, i.e. that the resolved model has no unexpected codimension-one points over the closed point of $\operatorname{Spec} O$; it is the site-level instance of the corresponding abstract gluing statement. It is used in the assembly of the resolved Deligne–Rapoport model together with its crossing charts, [`ModularCurve.DRModelPackage.exists_dRResolvedModelPackageV4_and_dRResolvedModelCharts`](thm.html#ModularCurve.DRModelPackage.exists_dRResolvedModelPackageV4_and_dRResolvedModelCharts).
